## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a constrained, real-time CV system that reasons about 3D pose, occlusion, and actionable outcomes (feasibility of mating for tool swaps) in an edge context with new hardware revisions.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 6-DoF pose for multiple components
- On-device adaptation (3-shot) to unseen revisions
- Occlusion-robust representation (2.5D priors)
- Tool-mating feasibility as a discriminative objective
- Synthetic+real data strategy and edge latency trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: pose and feasibility total loss
function totalLoss(posePred, poseGT, feasPred, feasGT, mask) {
  const poseDiff = posePred.sub(poseGT).mul(mask);
  const poseLoss = poseDiff.pow(2).sum() / mask.sum();
  const feasLoss = binaryCrossEntropy(feasPred, feasGT, mask);
  return poseLoss * 0.7 + feasLoss * 0.3;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would temporal consistency be enforced across frames on device?
- Which ablations show the impact of 2.5D priors vs full 3D reasoning on occlusion-heavy scenes?
